.TH ECHOPING 1
.SH NAME
echoping \- test a UDP echo service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B echoping
.RI HOST " [PORT [MESSAGE]]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolve HOST, send MESSAGE to its UDP echo service and compare the reply.
The default port is 7 and the default message is This is a test!.
Messages are limited to 1023 characters. A missing response times out after
five seconds. A failed lookup, timeout or differing reply returns nonzero.
The socket accepts replies only from the selected address and port.
.SH SEE ALSO
ping(1), host(1)
